<title>UK: Black Sea, Baltic oil exports up 629k bpd on week.</title>
<headline>Black Sea, Baltic oil exports up 629k bpd on week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals rose 629,730 barrels a day (bpd) to 2.08 million bpd in the third week of January from the previous week and a rise of 914,182 bpd over the same week last year, Petro-Logistics said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from the former Soviet Baltic and Black Sea ports rose 310,778 bpd on the week to 1.25 million bpd. This represented a rise of 738,594 bpd over the same period last year.</p>
<p>Fuel exports rose 65,486 bpd to 252,430 bpd were down 143,000 on the week at 168,000 bpd and 80,599 bpd higher than last year.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports were up 346,590 bpd to 392,621 bpd, a rise of 36,045 bpd over the same week last year. </p>
<p>Gasoline and jet exports combined were down 93,124 bpd at 63,720 bpd but up 76,006 bpd from the same time last year.</p>
